{"instruction_sha256":"30e1957fc0d939bf2eff852dc48a5c21826b4fecaead2eaffc45e4afcc161c7a","judge_config":{"claude":{"effort":"xhigh","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5"},"codex":{"effort":"xhigh","model":"gpt-6.1-sol"}},"kind":"grade","payload":{"passages":[{"passage_id":"11bd5b9328db0ed3380b05834a4ed440a250ef144bb7cba7ba16e9ba66f17d52","section_path":"Chapter 3. Basic Floating-Point Instructions > 3.2. Overview of Floating-Point Instructions > 3.2.4. Floating-Point Move Instructions > 3.2.4.1.** **`FMOV.{S/D}`","source_id":"loongarch-vol1","text":"#### **3.2.4.1.** **`FMOV.{S/D}`**\n\nInstruction formats:\n\n```\nfmov.s      fd, fj\nfmov.d      fd, fj\n```\n\n`FMOV{S/D}` writes the value of the floating-point register `fj` into the floating-point register `fd` in the singleprecision/double-precision floating-point number format. If the value of `fj` is not in the singleprecision/double-precision floating-point number format, the result is uncertain.\n\n```\nFMOV.S:\n    FR[fd][31:0] = FR[fj][31:0]\nFMOV.D:\n    FR[fd] = FR[fj]\n```\n\nThe above instruction operations are non-arithmetic and will not cause IEEE 754 exceptions, nor will they modify the Cause and Flags fields of the floating-point control and status register."},{"passage_id":"246b1324dd6ce98248e4d6ca28cfa3758791e9132997c59012592ab0647ad10d","section_path":"Table of Contents","source_id":"loongarch-vol1","text":"||\n|---|\n|3.2.3.2. FFINT{S/D}.{W/L}, FTINT.{W/L}.{S/D} . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 85|\n|3.2.3.3. FTINT{RM/RP/RZ/RNE}.{W/L}.{S/D} . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 87|\n|3.2.3.4. FRINT.{S/D}. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 89|\n|3.2.4. Floating-Point Move Instructions . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 90|\n|3.2.4.1. FMOV.{S/D} . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 90|\n|3.2.4.2. FSEL . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 91|\n|3.2.4.3. MOVGR2FR.{W/D}, MOVGR2FRH.W . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 91|\n|3.2.4.4. MOVFR2GR.{S/D}, MOVFRH2GR.S . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 92|\n|3.2.4.5. MOVGR2FCSR, MOVFCSR2GR . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 92|"},{"passage_id":"2cfa8cf7ff63be2d9ebec8e8fd991d23085b3837010aaa649121b379a483fd8d","section_path":"Table of Contents","source_id":"riscv-unprivileged","text":"||\n|---|\n|30.14.1. Vector Single-Width Integer Reduction Instructions ...................................................... 370|\n|30.14.2. Vector Widening Integer Reduction Instructions ............................................................ 371|\n|30.14.3. Vector Single-Width Floating-Point Reduction Instructions............................................ 371|\n|30.14.3.1. Vector Ordered Single-Width Floating-Point Sum Reduction.................................... 371|\n|30.14.3.2. Vector Unordered Single-Width Floating-Point Sum Reduction............................... 372|\n|30.14.3.3. Vector Single-Width Floating-Point Max and Min Reductions ................................. 373|\n|30.14.4. Vector Widening Floating-Point Reduction Instructions ................................................ 373|\n|30.15. Vector Mask Instructions....................................................................................................... 373|\n|30.15.1. Vector Mask-Register Logical Instructions...................................................................... 373|\n|30.15.2. Vector count population in mask vcpop.m ........................................................................ 375|\n|30.15.3. vfirst find-first-set mask bit........................................................................................... 375|\n|30.15.4. vmsbf.m set-before-first mask bit..................................................................................... 376|\n|30.15.5. vmsif.m set-including-first mask bit................................................................................. 376|\n|30.15.6. vmsof.m set-only-first mask bit ......................................................................................... 377|\n|30.15.7. Example using vector mask instructions......................................................................... 378|\n|30.15.8. Vector Iota Instruction ................................................................................................... 379|\n|30.15.9. Vector Element Index Instruction ................................................................................... 381|\n|30.16. Vector Permutation Instructions............................................................................................ 381|\n|30.16.1. Integer Scalar Move Instructions .................................................................................... 381|\n|30.16.2. Floating-Point Scalar Move Instructions......................................................................... 381|\n|30.16.3. Vector Slide Instructions................................................................................................ 382|\n|30.16.3.1. Vector Slideup Instructions...................................................................................... 382|\n|30.16.3.2. Vector Slidedown Instructions................................................................................. 383|\n|30.16.3.3. Vector Slide1up........................................................................................................ 383|\n|30.16.3.4. Vector Floating-Point Slide1up Instruction.............................................................. 384|\n|30.16.3.5. Vector Slide1down Instruction................................................................................. 384|\n|30.16.3.6. Vector Floating-Point Slide1down Instruction ......................................................... 385|\n|30.16.4. Vector Register Gather Instructions............................................................................... 385|\n|30.16.5. Vector Compress Instruction ......................................................................................... 386|\n|30.16.5.1. Synthesizing vdecompress........................................................................................... 387|\n|30.16.6. Whole Vector Register Move........................................................................................... 387|"},{"passage_id":"30f9f43610a491f2be77c2f293780b62e059c251a589f1a238aeb0e49d93397f","section_path":"Chapter 25. \"Zfa\" Extension for Additional Floating-Point Instructions, Version 1.0 > 25.5. Move Instructions","source_id":"riscv-unprivileged","text":"## **25.5. Move Instructions**\n\nFor RV32 only, if the D extension is implemented, the FMVH.X.D instruction moves bits 63:32 of floating-point register _rs1_ into integer register _rd_ . It is encoded in the OP-FP major opcode with _funct3_ =0, _rs2_ =1, and _funct7_ =1110001.\n\n _FMVH.X.D is used in conjunction with the existing FMV.X.W instruction to move adouble-precision floating-point number to a pair of x-registers._\n\nFor RV32 only, if the D extension is implemented, the FMVP.D.X instruction moves a double-precision number from a pair of integer registers into a floating-point register. Integer registers _rs1_ and _rs2_ supply bits 31:0 and 63:32, respectively; the result is written to floating-point register _rd_ . FMVP.D.X is encoded in the OP-FP major opcode with _funct3_ =0 and _funct7_ =1011001.\n\nFor RV64 only, if the Q extension is implemented, the FMVH.X.Q instruction moves bits 127:64 of floating-point register _rs1_ into integer register _rd_ . It is encoded in the OP-FP major opcode with _funct3_ =0, _rs2_ =1, and _funct7_ =1110011.\n\n _FMVH.X.Q is used in conjunction with the existing FMV.X.D instruction to move aquad-precision floating-point number to a pair of x-registers._\n\nFor RV64 only, if the Q extension is implemented, the FMVP.Q.X instruction moves a double-precision number from a pair of integer registers into a floating-point register. Integer registers _rs1_ and _rs2_ supply bits 63:0 and 127:64, respectively; the result is written to floating-point register _rd_ . FMVP.Q.X is encoded in the OP-FP major opcode with _funct3_ =0 and _funct7_ =1011011."}],"query":{"id":"q046","intent":"Find instructions that move floating-point bit representations between integer and floating-point registers.","text":"move raw bits between integer and floating-point registers"}},"pilot":false,"schema":{"$defs":{"Grade":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"architecture_tags":{"items":{"enum":["riscv","loongarch","x86","other"],"type":"string"},"title":"Architecture Tags","type":"array"},"grade":{"maximum":3,"minimum":0,"title":"Grade","type":"integer"},"passage_id":{"minLength":1,"title":"Passage Id","type":"string"},"quote":{"title":"Quote","type":"string"},"reason":{"minLength":1,"title":"Reason","type":"string"}},"required":["passage_id","grade","reason","quote","architecture_tags"],"title":"Grade","type":"object"}},"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"grades":{"items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Grade"},"title":"Grades","type":"array"}},"required":["grades"],"title":"GradeAnswer","type":"object"},"schema_version":3,"sha256":"d12fb34aefa5d26908a46f423b0b91bf7c0c44ab42e0c8641dfd39e288970e8b","system_sha256":"0731bfffd8dfd9b1a7f3394b7f28e0c875dbee813b796de4afe0936d756fea63"}
